For those who are not up on their siege engineering, a trebuchet is yet
another sort of catapult-like thing.  A _real_ catapult uses a spring of
some sort, typically a heavily torsioned set of ropes, for the motive
force.  An arbalest, mentioned in another post, uses a bow.  A trebuchet
uses a counterweight on a long, unequal arm.  You have the weight on one
end of the arm, and the carrying basket on the other.  You use ropes to
pull the basket down, stake 'em down, put your rock (or cow, or piano) into
the carrying basket, and cut the ropes.  Whoosh!

Fun for the whole family!


